---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions | SM Global Accounting Services"
  description="Terms of use for the SM Global Accounting Services website."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms &amp; Conditions</p>
      <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="lead">Last updated: [date]</p>

      <p class="placeholder-note" style="margin: var(--space-3) 0; max-width: none;">
        This page is a drafted starting template covering use of this website, not final legal text
        and not a client engagement contract. It has not been reviewed by a solicitor — get it
        checked before publishing, and note that actual client work is governed separately by each
        practice's engagement letter, not by this page.
      </p>

      <div class="grid" style="max-width: 760px; margin-top: var(--space-3);">
        <div>
          <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
          <p>
            These terms govern use of this website, operated by {SITE.name}
            ([legal entity name and registration details]). By using this site, you agree to them.
            If you don't agree, please don't use the site.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>2. This site is informational</h2>
          <p>
            Content on this site describes our services in general terms. It is not accounting, tax,
            or legal advice, and nothing on it forms a contract between us and you. A service
            engagement only begins once we've agreed scope, pricing, and terms directly with your
            practice in a separate engagement letter.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>3. Accuracy</h2>
          <p>
            We try to keep this site accurate and up to date, but we make no guarantee that every
            detail is current or error-free, and we may change the site's content at any time without
            notice.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>
          <p>
            The content, design, and branding on this site belong to {SITE.name} unless otherwise
            stated. You may view and print pages for your own reference, but you may not copy,
            republish, or reuse content from this site commercially without our written permission.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>5. Third-party links</h2>
          <p>
            This site may link to third-party websites (for example, software providers we work
            with). We don't control those sites and aren't responsible for their content or their
            own privacy practices.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>6. Liability</h2>
          <p>
            To the extent permitted by law, we aren't liable for any loss arising from your use of
            this website. This does not affect any liability that can't legally be excluded or
            limited. [Confirm final wording with a solicitor before publishing.]
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>7. Governing law</h2>
          <p>
            [Confirm before publishing: which country's law governs this website's terms, given the
            business is based in India and the audience is UK accountancy practices — this is a
            genuine choice to make with legal advice, not a default to leave unconfirmed.]
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>8. Changes to these terms</h2>
          <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date at the top will always reflect the current version.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>9. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
            See also our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
